  "question": {
    "text": "In an a.c. circuit, voltage and current are given by: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math> respectively. The average power dissipated in one cycle is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XJhHY",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>",
